index 4479b53..a420bbb 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,35 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Open `/devtools-times/account` from the header to manage your account. Password
+sign-in is verified by the existing Times login service; successful sign-in now
+creates a server-side session. Readers can add passkeys, rename their labels,
+remove them, and update the account display name. Passkeys created here can also
+be used from the sign-in page. All credential mutations require an authenticated
+session and a matching request origin.
+
+Requires Node.js 22.13 or newer. Account profiles and verified public credentials
+are stored in SQLite at `./data/accounts.sqlite`; set `ACCOUNT_DB_PATH` to use a
+persistent disk location. The default Astro Node session driver also uses local
+filesystem storage. Deploy with persistent storage for both, and use shared
+storage before running multiple application instances. Existing remote accounts
+are linked on their next successful password sign-in; the remote service does
+not expose a passkey inventory endpoint, so this page manages credentials
+registered by this application.
+
+Passkeys require HTTPS (or localhost). Set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the canonical public
+origin (for example, `https://news.example.com`) when running behind a proxy;
+otherwise the request URL origin is used. Keep the origin and hostname stable
+because credentials are scoped to the hostname. Registration and authentication
+verify the challenge, origin, relying party, and user verification on the server.
+
+The page sends the complete accepted credential list to supported password
+managers on load and after removal. Account display-name updates use WebAuthn's
+`signalCurrentUserDetails`; per-key labels are local account metadata because
+WebAuthn has no signal to rename an individual credential. Unsupported or failed
+sync leaves the saved account change intact and offers manual guidance and retry.
+See the [WebAuthn Signal API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/webauthn-signal-api)
+and [SimpleWebAuthn server documentation](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server).
